    "blurb": "The show shines in its second half where a concise Play In The Band flows into China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider and erupts into an inspired Truckin' > Eyes Of The World jam. Keith’s piano work adds texture to the extended improvisation, and the band keeps the momentum high throughout.",
    "review": "March 30, 1973 at Rochester's Community War Memorial Auditorium finds the Dead in fine form, especially after the first set’s modestly recorded opening. The second set kicks off with a tight Play In The Band that segues into an uplifting China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider before launching into a powerful Truckin' > Eyes Of The World sequence that stands out as the night’s highlight. Keith Godchaux’s piano accents during the jam give it a distinctive flavor, while Jerry’s lead lines and Phil’s bass underpin the improvisation with confidence. Though the early portion of the matrix recording is muddy, the clean soundboard feed captures the band’s high‑energy interplay and makes this show worth revisiting for anyone who loves 1973-era Dead magic.",
